{
  "about": "Shared barcode-weight cases (Mevaser 28/10 barcode-vs-OCR weight check). The same file lives in the bot repo (tests/fixtures/barcode_weight_fixture.json) and the scanner repo (test/fixtures/barcode_weight_fixture.json); every implementation (bot/utils/carton_barcode.py, lib/barcode-weight.ts, SQL carton_barcode_weight_kg) must return family/kg exactly as listed. family = gs31 | glatt25 | null (no barcode weight); kg = weight in kg or null. class is descriptive only. source: db = a real box_inventory barcode, synthetic = a bound or shape case.",
  "spec": {
    "gs31": "strip a leading \"]C1\", then ^\\d{31}$; kg = int(chars 14-18, 1-based)/100; valid 0.5 < kg <= 100; char 19 is a per-batch digit",
    "glatt25": "^1(\\d{5})(110010|010010|110610)(\\d{4})(\\d{9})$; kg = int(group 3)/100; valid 0.5 < kg <= 60; mid 140010 = units, any other mid = no weight",
    "agree": "|ocr_kg - barcode_kg| < 0.01 kg (exactly 0.01 is a difference)"
  },
